    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d126">

                <pb facs="1148" n="990" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg990"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Japanese Chargé to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Japan</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-04-03"><hi rendition="#italic">April 3,
                        1906</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 21.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you under
                    instructions that the Japanese Government desires to establish a reciprocal
                    exemption of steamboat inspection as between the vessels of Japan and the United
                    States under the provisions of section 4400, United States Revised Statutes, and
                    that the Japanese Government are prepared to issue orders exempting United
                    States vessels from inspection upon the assurance that the United States
                    Government will issue similar orders exempting Japanese vessels.</p>
                <p>I inclose herewith a copy each of the English translation of “ship-inspection law
                    “and” ship-inspection regulations” of Japan now in force.<anchor n="d"
                        xml:id="d126-f1"/></p>
                <p>It is desired that the above proposition may receive prompt and favorable
                    consideration of the United States Government.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eki Hioki.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
